Player-discovered emergent combinations. Players will find combinations the simulation didn't test. Some of these will be unbalanced. The 85% target is for combinations within the simulated space; combinations outside that space are unknown until players discover them.

The mitigation is: simulation has to be thorough enough that the unsimulated space is small. This means simulating not just "gear A on kit B" but "gear A and gear C and gear D on kit B doing content E." The combinatorial explosion that makes traditional balance hard makes simulation thoroughness hard.

