What you're proposing is a different kind of metric — peak performance moments. The KPM-over-100 spike. The optimal three minutes of concentrated play. The "this is how good I can get when everything aligns" moment.

Peak moments are democratizing because they're not gated by time investment. A casual player who plays 30 minutes per day might hit a KPM spike during one perfect run. A hardcore player who plays 6 hours per day might also hit a similar peak. The peak doesn't reflect hours played; it reflects skill of preparation and optimal execution of the moment.

This is structurally different from how ARPG bragging currently works. Most current ARPG bragging is cumulative ("I've farmed X currency over Y hours") or completion-based ("I cleared Z content"). Peak moments are performative ("look what I achieved in this moment").

